{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1505548-struggling-to-name-a-cabal","id":1505548,"title":"Struggling to name a cabal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-17T08:55:45-07:00","id":1505548,"title":"Struggling to name a cabal","content":"Gaaahh!! Naming this one particular cabal has been stymieing me for <i><u><b>weeks</b></u></i> now! Like....I know the members, I know their general philosophical theme, I just can't figure out how to distill/combine those into one particular name XD :sob: :sob: :sob: :sob:<br /> <br /> The cabal is meant, narratively speaking, to be a counterpoint to the Whipping Boys cabal ~ the WB are mostly Arrows &amp; mostly Obrimos and have their own unique Legacy centered around the bodily experience of pain (yes, like that ~ they're sadomasochists).<br /> <br /> The cabal I'm trying to name is much more diverse and is focused more on Dominance/submission play than on sadomasochism. Of course, their leader is in the Concord of Serpents, so don't think they go easy! But their whole philosophy is about submitting to another being as a way to rid yourself of your assumed lacks and limitations, the sacredness of the D/s relationship and how that can be leveraged for self-growth. They also administer the Bay Area's kink Labyrinth, as the Whipping Boys are (a) the wrong order and (b) more interested in having fun/fighting/enlightenment than doing that kind of work<br /> <br /> Members:<br /> <b>Kushiel</b> (angel who punishes sinners in Hell), Mastigos Guardian of the Veil in the Concord of Serpents, Dominant<br /> <b>Ninshubur</b> (the goddess Inanna's vizier/bodyguard/servant deity), Moros Quiescent in the Guardians of the Veil, submissive (to a Sleeper, actually)<br /> <b>Vahana</b> (the animal mounts/companions of Hindu gods), Thyrsus Daksha mystagogue, submissive<br /> <b>Permission</b>, Obrimos thearch in the Bene Ashmedai, switch\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T09:29:25-07:00","id":1505550,"title":"","content":"Graven Suzerainty. The oath of vassaldom establishes certain duties and responsibilities of the suzereran, whereas the graven part would seem like something members of the Concord of Serpents and Bene Asmodai would come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-17-2023, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T11:09:48-07:00","id":1505569,"title":"","content":"ABSA: As Below, So Above","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T16:14:09-07:00","id":1505607,"title":"","content":"Both of those are REALLY GOOD options. Much better than anything I've come up with XD<br /> <br /> Well . . . except for calling this cabal &quot;the Sword Bridge&quot; ~ mebbe &quot;the Sword Bridge Society&quot;? &quot;Club Swordbridge&quot;?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I remembered a bit from <i>Lancelot, Knight of the Cart</i>, in which Lancelot has to cross a bridge made of a giant sword in order to rescue Guinevere from King meleagant:<br /> &quot;They stopped and dismounted at the foot<br /> Of the terrifying structure, looking<br /> Down at the treacherous water,<br /> Black and boiling, swift<br /> And harsh, as horribly evil<br /> As if it flowed from the devil<br /> Himself, deep and dangerous<br /> Like nothing else in this world:<br /> Whoever fell in would sink<br /> Like a rock in the salty sea.<br /> And the bridge that spanned it was just<br /> As different from other bridges;<br /> Believe me, nothing lie it<br /> Had ever existed, or ever<br /> Would, neither as huge<br /> Or as wickedly built-a single<br /> Gleaming sword-blade crossing<br /> That ice-cold water, stiff<br /> And strong, as wide as a pair<br /> Of spears, and attached at either<br /> End to massive tree-trunk<br /> Stumps. No one would worry<br /> About it bending or breaking:<br /> It would clearly stand, no matter<br /> What weight it was asked to bear.<br /> But those who\u2019d come with our knight<br /> Were most concerned at seeing,<br /> Or thinking they saw, a pair<br /> Of lions, or perhaps they were leopards,<br /> Chained to a boulder on the far<br /> Side of the bridge. [ . . . ]<br /> I know quite well you wish me<br /> To come to no harm. But my faith<br /> In God, my trust in Him,<br /> Compels me to believe Hell protect me.<br /> Neither bridge nor water<br /> Nor this harsh world can worry<br /> Me. I intend to cross,<br /> Whatever the risk. I\u2019d rather<br /> Die than turn and go back!\u201d<br /> There was nothing more to be said,<br /> But pity and sorrow wrung them<br /> Both with bitter tears.<br /> And our knight made ready, as best<br /> He could, to cross the gulf,<br /> Preparing, in the strangest way,<br /> By removing the armor from his hands<br /> And feet, as if making sure<br /> He could not arrive uninjured!<br /> Then he held tight to the sword-blade<br /> Bridge, as sharp as a razor,<br /> Hands and feet both bare<br /> For he\u2019d left himself no covering,<br /> Neither shoes nor stockings<br /> Not fearing sharp edges slicing<br /> Away at his flesh, much<br /> Preferring bloody wounds<br /> To falling into that icy<br /> Water from which he would never<br /> Emerge. Accepting the immense<br /> Pain and suffering, he crossed,<br /> Hands and knees and feet<br /> Bleeding. But Love, who had led him<br /> There, helped him as he went,<br /> And turned his pain to pleasure.<br /> When he came to the other side<br /> None of his wounds were hurting.<br /> And then he recalled the pair<br /> Of lions he\u2019d seen, or thought<br /> He\u2019d seen, before he crossed,<br /> But looking here and there<br /> All he could see was a lizard,<br /> And nothing there that could harm him<br /> Raising his hand to his face<br /> He stared at his ring, and knew<br /> At once the pair of lions<br /> Were imagined, and nowhere in sight,<br /> But conjured out of magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> It really feels like it sums up the philosophical orientation of the cabal in a very magely way, the same kind of pretentiosity that mages who take names like &quot;Kushiel&quot; and &quot;Ninshubur&quot; would be attracted to.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Better suggestions?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T17:24:33-07:00","id":1505612,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a passage a mentor of the Fallen Pillar might use to illustrate the philosophy to his student. It seem like a middle ground between both cabal's philosophies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}